  "note": "This scene is the location. Shots 2 and 3 take the deck, parapet, bay lines, masts and the car's parked position from here unchanged, so three clips read as one place. The skyline is deliberately absent for now -- tried and set aside, not forgotten; above the parapet there is nothing, and what goes there comes from the prompt. Shot 1, laid out against the reference frame: car parked side-on and left of centre at about 16 m, subtending a sixth of frame height; she walks away right of centre at about 6 m, a little over a third of it. Both fall out of a 35 mm lens at those distances, which is how the lens was chosen rather than picked. The aim sits on the car and stays there -- it is the one thing in frame that does not move, and tracking her instead is what kept centring her. She does not reach the car: the shot ends nine metres short of it.",
